        {
            "id": "29697460",
            "user": "Seymour Edits",
            "timestamp": "18:01, 29 June 2021",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(8,353 bytes)",
            "change": 195,
            "summary": "(NCA edit. Do not revert.)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "revert",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Attend a trade school or vocational school. The courses offered at trade and vocational schools provide important preparation for entering an electrician apprenticeship program.<ref>[v161834_b01]. 21 June 2021.</ref>[[Image:Become a Licensed Electrician Step 5 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Enter an electrician apprentice program. Most states require at least two years, and in most cases up to four years, of apprenticeship with a master or licensed electrician before one can take the examination to become a licensed electrician. During an apprenticeship, one earns the title of [[Become a Journeyman Electrician (US)|journeyman electrician]]. Many apprenticeships combine hands-on experience with classroom instruction.<ref>[v161834_b01]. 21 June 2021.</ref> Some organizations that sponsor or provide apprentice programs through local chapters include:[[Image:Become a Licensed Electrician Step 6 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Study the [http://www.nfpa.org/aboutthecodes/AboutTheCodes.asp?DocNum=70&cookie_test=1 National Electrical Code]. In order to get licensed to work as an electrician in most states, you will have to demonstrate knowledge of the National Electrical Code, which lays out laws, regulations and other information about safe practices.<ref>[v161834_b01]. 21 June 2021.</ref>[[Image:Become a Licensed Electrician Step 7 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Get a state license. Most states require that you get a state license in order to practice as an electrician. The license is granted after taking an exam to demonstrate knowledge of the National Electrical Code and local electrical and building codes. In order to take the exam:<ref>[v161834_b01]. 21 June 2021.</ref>[[Image:Become a Licensed Electrician Step 8 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Get certified. Choose from a variety of specialized certifications to enhance your career. Certifications vary by state and will help you pursue work as an electrical administrator, a telecommunications contractor, or a specialist in an area like instrumentation.<ref>[v161834_b01]. 21 June 2021.</ref>[[Image:Become a Licensed Electrician Step 10 Version 3.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Attend a trade school or vocational school. The courses offered at trade and vocational schools provide important preparation for entering an electrician apprenticeship program.[[Image:Become a Licensed Electrician Step 5 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Enter an electrician apprentice program. Most states require at least two years, and in most cases up to four years, of apprenticeship with a master or licensed electrician before one can take the examination to become a licensed electrician. During an apprenticeship, one earns the title of [[Become a Journeyman Electrician (US)|journeyman electrician]]. Many apprenticeships combine hands-on experience with classroom instruction. Some organizations that sponsor or provide apprentice programs through local chapters include:[[Image:Become a Licensed Electrician Step 6 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Study the [http://www.nfpa.org/aboutthecodes/AboutTheCodes.asp?DocNum=70&cookie_test=1 National Electrical Code]. In order to get licensed to work as an electrician in most states, you will have to demonstrate knowledge of the National Electrical Code, which lays out laws, regulations and other information about safe practices.[[Image:Become a Licensed Electrician Step 7 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Get a state license. Most states require that you get a state license in order to practice as an electrician. The license is granted after taking an exam to demonstrate knowledge of the National Electrical Code and local electrical and building codes. In order to take the exam,[[Image:Become a Licensed Electrician Step 8 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Get certified. Choose from a variety of specialized certifications to enhance your career. Certifications vary by state and will help you pursue work as an electrical administrator, a telecommunications contractor, or a specialist in an area like instrumentation.[[Image:Become a Licensed Electrician Step 10 Version 3.jpg|center]]"
                ]
            }
        },
